/**
 * The same piece open in more than one tab.
 *
 * Every tab on the editor joins one BroadcastChannel. When a tab saves a
 * manuscript it tells the others, with a version vector saying which saves
 * the manuscript already contains. A tab showing that piece then either
 *
 * - brings the change in by itself, when it has no edits of its own and the
 *   new version contains what it shows (the common case: writing in one tab,
 *   coming back to the other), or
 * - says so, when both tabs changed the piece: the writer can preview what
 *   changed, bring it in paragraph by paragraph, or keep this tab's version.
 *
 * Nothing is lost silently. A version about to be saved over without having
 * been brought in is kept in Versions first, and so is a stored version a
 * save finds in its way that no broadcast announced (a tab from an older
 * build, or a message still in flight).
 */
