# Scrolling during model runs

Branch: `fix/flicker-during-model-runs`.
Base: v0.27.1, `bae99e2b4c24d689b6ec425cf444b3f3814c0e3e`.

## Reproduction and fixes

Three concurrent local BYOK streams updated three anchored margin replies while a
180-paragraph manuscript scrolled for 10 seconds. The browser used the real AI SDK,
persona feedback/analysis functions, editor note event handlers, conductor, and
margin surface. IndexedDB supplied a local provider; external requests were blocked.

The cards did **not** remount as new elements. Their existing DOM nodes repeatedly
moved through the keyed list. `onReplyStream` reset `createdAt` on every token;
freshness ranking therefore changed on every interleaved stream update. DOM
reinsertion replayed the cards' entrance animations. The timestamp now changes
once when a reply starts: `src/components/editor/extensions/flow-conductor.ts:1323`
and `:1339`. Entrance animations and live replies remain enabled.

Incoming persona notes also changed the writer's selection to each quotation.
`src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx:2416` now batches annotations through
`src/components/editor/extensions/persona-note-mark.ts:123`. The transaction keeps
the selection, requests no scrolling, adds no prose undo step, and avoids dispatch
for identical re-delivery. The regression test verifies all four properties.

Live and quick review wrongly required a Convex client before reaching the
writer's own judgement endpoint. They now let the existing `askJudgement` transport
choose the route: `src/utils/live-review.ts:162` and
`src/components/editor/extensions/quick-review.ts:239`. The signed-out probe reaches
its loopback endpoint and reports the deliberately injected outage, rather than
asking the writer to connect an account.

Live-review retries previously cleared a visible problem on `waiting`/`reading`,
then inserted it again when the retry failed. Independent quick/live failures
could also replace each other. `src/components/writing-tools/live-review-status.tsx:53`
and `:118`, with `src/utils/review-notices.ts:9`, retain an unresolved notice until
its own feed succeeds or pauses. The existing dismiss action still works.

Three SSR warnings named `q-e:qvisible`, `useVisibleTask$`, and the
`intersection-observer` strategy on components with no DOM root. Their listeners
now explicitly use `document-ready`:

- `src/utils/auth-context.tsx:289`
- `src/components/knowledge/account-tool-review.tsx:33`
- `src/components/desk/public-desk.tsx:98`

A subsequent editor HTML request emitted none of those warnings. No blanket
animation disabling or global warning suppression was added.

## Before and after

One valid matching pair per browser, 10 seconds each, development build,
1920 × 1080 viewport. These are local single-run observations, not a general
throughput benchmark.

| Measurement                                | Firefox before → after | Chromium before → after |
| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------------- |
| Existing card-node reinsertions            | 47 → 0                 | 33 → 0                  |
| New card-node remounts                     | 0 → 0                  | 0 → 0                   |
| Layout-shift entries                       | API unavailable        | 20 → 14                 |

